How this router is reached over the network.

A box nobody has set up refuses to be configured over the network at
all: the web UI is served, and every other request is turned away.
That is what lets olr open the UI the moment it is installed without
leaving an unprotected admin API on your LAN.

Setting it up is `olr claim`, once. There is no user model here — one
box, one optional password, no accounts.

Usage:
  olr system [command]

Available Commands:
  set         Change administrator access
  show        Show how this router may be reached

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for system

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")

Use "olr system [command] --help" for more information about a command.
